  {
    "number": 64,
    "title": "Add Monitor controls and shared display ownership",
    "body": "Refs #33\n\nAdds a Monitor panel with owner-backed label and notice actions, project/session filters and exact RGB preview. Explicit Monitor activation pauses the retained playlist; Media selection leaves it paused, while start/resume selects Media. Agent events continue in either mode without taking over the display.\n\nMonitor pictures use Player's sole adapter and serialized queue, generation cancellation, latest-view coalescing and the qualified 1000 ms default cadence. Restart and screen-on remain passive. A finite authenticated `pixoo-integration/1.0` extension shares guarded commands and receipts with the browser while preserving released controller v1 and existing MCP tools.\n\nValidation at `0f6415f65dfe971b04b23bc178c4217dd15db24a`:\n- Node 24 `npm ci`, `npm run check`: 582 tests in 62 files and 10 workflow fixtures.\n- `npm run test:browser`: 58 desktop/mobile checks, including exact preview pixels. An earlier run hit a static-page 404 during a concurrent rebuild; a full run with stable assets passed unchanged.\n- Focused tests cover delayed/uncertain transport, cancellation, cadence/bursts, Media preservation, competing clients, replay/conflicts, revoked native streams and selected-owner cutover/rollback. Initial red runs preceded writer, API and panel implementation.\n- OpenSpec synchronized and archived: 17 current specifications, 18 archives. Both workflow checks and `git diff --check` pass.\n\nSource-only. No installation or device operation. Integrated client/physical acceptance remains #34. Cancellation can leave a started physical request applied; the service retains uncertainty and performs no automatic retry. [Hub guide companion #119](https://github.com/jimmie-potts/agent-device-hub/pull/119) is a draft owned by this coordinator; guide synchronization remains pending until it merges. Public guide publication is outside this delivery.\n\nIndependent Standards and Specification reviews, all five current PR jobs, guarded merge and all five merged-main jobs remain required before issue closure. Implementation used one coordinating writer; two independent high-impact reviewers are requested as Astra/high. Usage is unknown.\n",
    "state": "open",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/jimmie-potts/divoom-app-upgrade/pull/64",
